DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     544      0     65  Mixed  You destroy our factories and bases. Why should we deal with you?
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     570      0     69  Title  We will not talk of it while you are amassing ships near our borders.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     571      0    101  Mixed  Remove your ships along our borders and we will consider accepting. Until then we are not interested.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     572      0     70  Mixed  Your fleets intrude on \x81 space. Move them away, then we shall talk.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     573      0     87  Mixed  Your ships on our borders are no threat to us. But we refuse to deal while they remain.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     574      0     84  Title  If you wish to deal with the \x81s, then send your ships to threaten others, not us.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     585      0     84  Mixed  You attack our ships without provocation and expect us to accept? We refuse to deal.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     586      0     58  Title  We cannot accept an offer from one who attacks our fleets.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     587      0     58  Title  Once your fleets have stopped attacking ours, we can talk.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     588      0     64  Title  If you wish to deal with the \x81s, then leave our fleets alone.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     589      0     82  Mixed  Emperor \x89 does not appreciate your destruction of our fleets. We do not accept.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     600      0     89  Mixed  We have not forgotten the attack on the \x85 colony. There is no way that we will accept.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1     601      0     85  Mixed  The dead of \x85 cry out for retribution. We hear their cries louder than your offer.
