DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1110      0     80  Mixed  We tire of diplomatic negotiations. We can continue discussions at a later time.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1111      0     51  Mixed  These talks get us nowhere. We must take our leave.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1112      0     57  Mixed  Emperor \x89 has heard enough. We will talk again later.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1113      0     73  Mixed  Emperor \x83, you try our patience. Perhaps you should speak again later.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1114      0     58  Mixed  A thousand apologies, Emperor \x83, but other duties call.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1115      0     68  Mixed  We have little time and much to do. Perhaps we can talk again later.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1116      0     80  Mixed  The \x80s are creatures of much wind and little action. We tire of your prattle.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1117      0     10  Title  We go now.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1118      0     37  Title  Pardon us, but our time is at an end.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1125      0     42  Title  You have no technology which interests us.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1126      0     29  Title  We have no need of \x80 toys.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1127      0     45  Title  Your primitive inventions do not interest us.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1128      0     42  Title  The \x81s are far beyond your technology.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1129      0     68  Title  Emperor \x83, we have little need for what your scientists offer us.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1130      0     56  Title  Emperor \x89 sees little of interest in your technology.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1140      0    105  Mixed  The \x92s have declared war on our empire. Will you honor our alliance and assault the treacherous \x92s?
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1141      0    114  Mixed  The \x92s have declared war on our empire. Will you honor our alliance and join forces to battle our common enemy?
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1155      0     58  Mixed  You have dishonored the agreement. The alliance is broken.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1156      0     76  Mixed  Very well. Your untrustworthy intentions have shown. The alliance is broken.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1157      0     77  Mixed  We have little need of treaties that are not honored. The alliance is broken.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1158      0     33  Mixed  So be it. The alliance is broken.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1170      0    126  Mixed  Yes, Emperor \x83, the time has come for both our empires to strike out against the \x92s and eliminate them once and for all.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1171      0     56  Title  The \x80s and \x81s must unite to strike down the \x92s.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1172      0     75  Title  The \x92 empire must fall before the combined might of the \x80s and \x81s.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1173      0     58  Title  With \x81s and \x80s allied, the \x92s will not last long.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1174      0     93  Mixed  In the year \x8F, the \x81 and \x80 empires join forces to rid the galaxy of the \x92 menace.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1175      0     98  Mixed  In view of the threat from the \x92 Empire, the \x80 and \x81 empires have no choice but to unite!
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1185      0     57  Title  We are not amused that you have cast your lot against us.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1186      0     95  Mixed  How could you vote for the vain \x86s? If you continue to rouse my ire, you will know my wrath.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1187      0    155  Mixed  We have learned to keep our friends close and our enemies even closer. Vote against me again in the Galactic Council and we may be within laser distance...
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1188      0    152  Mixed  Your vote cast against the \x81 race has made us a mockery throughout the galaxy. We will not soon forget the humiliation that you have wrought upon us.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1189      0    144  Mixed  As your Galactic Council vote indicates, those who are not for us are against us. Consider yourself moved up several places on our to kill list.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1190      0    135  Mixed  Et tu, \x83 Beware, for if I should pluck your dagger from my back, I know how to weild it and will teach you to vote against me again.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1191      0    109  Mixed  You realize, of course, the power I wield, and I will squash you like an insect for your electoral treachery.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1192      0     74  Title  There are penalties for voting against the \x81, as you may soon find out.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1193      0    104  Mixed  Stabbed in the back, right under my nose! Your voting record reads like a political assassin's handbook.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1194      0    125  Title  If your vile attacks on our good reputation continue, we shall write your deceitful little handbook a most unpleasant ending.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1195      0    145  Mixed  While deceit becomes you, our patience is wearing thin. Casting votes against the \x81 race is the sort of mistake that should only be made once.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1200      0    108  Title  Although we did not win the election, we are most pleased that you decided to cast your votes with the \x81.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1201      0    120  Mixed  Well, \x83, this could be the beginning of a beautiful friendship. Thanks for your vote in the Galactic Council meeting.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1202      0    109  Mixed  We are pleased with your voting. With your continued enlightened voting, Emperor \x89 shall unite the galaxy.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1203      0    127  Mixed  We are flattered that you have voted for the \x81 s. You must pay us a formal visit very soon. Perhaps we can return the favor.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1204      0    120  Mixed  You show wisdom in casting your votes with us. Despite our natural misgivings, perhaps we will have a prosperous future.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1205      0    110  Mixed  We take your vote for us as clear gesture that you wish to improve your relations with the mighty \x81 Empire.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1206      0     81  Mixed  Hurrah! And remember, a vote for \x89 is a vote for galactic peace and stability.
DIPLOMAT.LBX      1    1207      0    106  Title  Although we greatly appreciate your vote, the cynics among us wonder what strings might be attached to it.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0       0      0    133  Mixed  A virulent plague has broken out on \x80. The disease has the potential to kill millions. Scientists need to research to find a cure.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0       1      0    140  Mixed  The plague continues on \x80. \x81 million colonists died last year. Scientists believe that they are \x82 research points away from a cure.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0       2      0     87  Mixed  Scientists have found the cure for the plague on \x80. The pestilence will finally end.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0       4      0     97  Mixed  A virulent plague has struck the \x84 colony on \x80. Millions of colonists fear for their lives.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0       5      0     90  Mixed  \x84 scientists finally found a cure for the \x80 plague. The pestilence will finally end.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0       7      0    100  Title  A violent quake hit the colony on \x80 killing \x81 million colonists and destroying \x82 factories.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      11      0    105  Title  A violent quake hit the \x84 colony on \x80 killing \x81 million colonists and destroying \x82 factories.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      14      0    162  Mixed  Scientists predict that the star in the \x80 system will go super nova within \x81 year\x83. If a research solution cannot be found, the colony will be destroyed.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      15      0    130  Mixed  Only \x81 year\x83 remain\x8D before the \x80 star goes super nova. Scientists still need \x82 research points to find a solution.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      16      0    108  Title  Scientists on \x80 have developed a solar rejuvenator thus ending the threat of their star going super nova.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      17      0     89  Title  The star in \x80 has gone super nova, destroying most of the planet and killing millions.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      18      0     90  lower  \x84 scientists are predicting that their star in the \x80 system will soon go super nova.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      19      0    110  lower  \x84 scientists managed to save the \x80 colony by inventing and using a solar rejuvenator on the star's core.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      20      0     90  Title  The star \x80 has gone super nova destroying most of the \x84 colony and killing millions.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      21      0    143  Mixed  A major industrial accident on \x80 has irradiated the entire planet. The intense radiation levels threaten to kill millions unless cleaned up.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      22      0    119  Title  The radiation from the industrial accident on \x80 has been cleaned up, but the ecology has already been badly damaged.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      25      0    147  Mixed  A major industrial accident on the \x84 colony of \x80 has irradiated the entire planet. The intense pollution levels will certainly kill millions.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      26      0     84  Title  The radiation from the \x84 industrial accident on \x80 has been finally cleaned up.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      28      0    156  Mixed  Without sanction the \x84 ambassador attempted to assassinate emperor \x8C and failed. His motives are unclear, but personal revenge may have been involved.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      35      0    142  Mixed  An insidious computer virus struck the main \x86 research network destroying \x82 research points. It may take years to recover from the loss.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      39      0    147  Mixed  An insidious computer virus struck the \x84 main \x86 research network destroying \x82 research points. It may take years to recover from the loss.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      42      0    163  Mixed  Astronomers predict that a comet will collide with the \x80 colony within \x81 year\x83. Unless the star fleet can destroy the comet, the colony will be destroyed.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      43      0    100  Title  Our fleet has destroyed \x82 percent of the comet due to strike our colony on \x80 in \x81 year\x83.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      44      0     80  Title  Our glorious star fleet has destroyed the comet that threatened the \x80 system.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      45      0     56  Title  The dreaded comet has utterly destroyed the \x80 colony.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      46      0    170  Mixed  \x84 astronomers predict that a comet will collide with the \x80 colony within \x81 year\x83. Unless their star fleet can destroy the comet, the colony will be destroyed.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      47      0    124  Title  The \x84 star fleet managed to destroy the comet threatening the \x80 system before it could inflict damage on their colony.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      48      0     61  Title  The dreaded comet has utterly destroyed the \x84 \x80 colony.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      49      0    148  Mixed  Pirates based in the \x80 star system have begun disrupting trade routes. More ships are needed to patrol the area if the pirates are to be stopped.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      50      0    146  Mixed  Pirate activity in the \x80 system reduced annual trade revenues by \x81 percent last year. Merchants are demanding more ships to patrol the area.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      51      0     60  Title  Pirate activity in the \x80 star system has been eliminated.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      53      0     90  Title  Pirates based in the \x80 star system have begun raiding and disrupting \x84 trade routes.
EVENTMSG.LBX      0      54      0     74  Title  The \x84 fleet has managed to erradicate the pirates plaguing their trade.
